# Per-contributor agent instructions. These describe how one person's tooling
# should behave in this repo, not how the repo works — nothing in the tree
# cites either file. Keeping them untracked lets each contributor carry their
# own without a diff every time someone's differs.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Agent CLI working state. Both of these run inside this repo — codex under
# `codex exec -C`, claude in the worktrees the fleet creates — and each drops
# a local directory of settings and session state that is nobody else's
# business. Ignored here rather than in a personal global excludes file, so a
# contributor who has not set one up does not find them in `git status`.
.claude/
.codex/
